The correct retry invariant is that, immediately before every attempt, desired equals expected + 1. expected need not still match the counter: a mismatch causes failure and refreshes expected, after which we recompute desired. A spurious failure also just triggers another iteration; only a successful comparison ends the operation, and that success replaces the matched value with its successor.

